# These files are not interchangeable between line endings.
#
# `overrides/*.patch` are unified diffs with three lines of context. Git on
# Windows defaults to converting text to CRLF on checkout; a diff converted that
# way no longer applies to the LF tree it was generated from, and `git apply`
# fails with "patch does not apply". The seam test catches it, but the failure
# only shows up in a fresh clone — exactly the situation a sync happens in.
#
# `sync-skills.py` renormalises to LF as a second guard, so either alone would
# be enough. Both are cheap and they fail differently.
*.patch text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
*.mjs text eol=lf
*.ts text eol=lf
*.js text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf

# Built output is compared byte-for-byte by the seam test.
lib/** -text
